Dear Tom,

I would do this:
fill up your data array for the detection/nondetections with NAs for those surveys that are missing relative to a protocol where all sites have the same number of surveys
then, you organize the observational covariates in arrays of the exact same dimension, but instead of NAs you fill in any number, e.g., a 0.
This should work. If you have very large data sets and very large number of zeroes, then this approach is wasteful and something slightly more refined is needed.

Best regards  -- Marc

